<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The chipsets Google Play delivers the NPU modules to (../npu/): a module
  installs with the app only on a phone in one of its device groups, so a
  chipset missing here gets no NPU libraries and lists no NPU.  Play matches
  the exact pair the phone reports (ro.soc.manufacturer, ro.soc.model, API
  31+): no wildcard, no vendor-only selector.  Keep it current, as
  app/AGENTS.md (NPU delivery) says.

  Qualcomm: one group per Hexagon generation, which picks the Skel/Stub
  module (qualcomm_runtime_vNN) beside the shared qualcomm_runtime.  The
  generations are LiteRT's own (litert/vendors/qualcomm/supported_soc.csv,
  v2.2.0): every row at v68 or later, less automotive (SA*) parts; v65/v66
  rows have no HTP.  SC8380XP is Snapdragon X Elite, in the Snapdragon
  Googlebooks (Android laptops).  Each chipset is listed under both
  manufacturer names, as LiteRT's AI Pack export does: Play cannot tell
  "Qualcomm" from "QTI".

  Google Tensor: G3 and later, the chipsets LiteRT's Tensor module serves
  (litert/python/aot/vendors/google_tensor/target.py).
-->
<config:device-targeting-config xmlns:config="http://schemas.android.com/apk/config">

    <config:device-group name="qualcomm_v68">
        <config:device-selector>
            <config:system-on-chip manufacturer="QTI" model="QCM6490"/>
